If a patient has a negative-toxicology-test for a prescribed-opioid then the negative-toxicology-test may indicate a prescribed-opioid-nonuse for the patient.
If a patient has a negative-toxicology-test for a prescribed-opioid and a clinician reviews the negative-toxicology-test then the clinician should consider a false-negative-test-result and should consider a test-result-misinterpretation.
